A||||2||Robert||It’s still not to late for a good idea…..||||10||
Z||000000||Robert||01-01-2001||07:33 PM||||Now that most of us have a Fiero calendar, I thought I would pass this along.<BR>A number of years ago I heard a local disk jockey say that one of the things he always did on the first day of the year was to write down his cars mileage on the wall calendar. <BR>It’s not all that hard to do, and the payoff next year is interesting.  Now don’t get me wrong, I’m not the type to write down my mileage every time I fill the tank, I hate it when I have to wait in the gas line while someone is doing all his or her paperwork.<BR>What I found out this January 1st is that I drove my Fiero 4,241 miles, my Camry 17,270 miles and my old truck 2,648 miles.<BR>Try it; I think you’ll like it.<P><P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/T2.GIF"> <P> “If you don’t look for that parking space near the entrance, you’ll never get it”||||reg||10
Z||000001||Songman||01-01-2001||07:40 PM||||Good idea, Robert... I may try that...<P>I think you need to get out and ride around more though. Those are some low miles!||||reg||1
